WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.334
Invitations and Celebrations.

2
00:00:02.614 --> 00:00:06.966
Day 56 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.716 --> 00:00:09.740
The key idea.

4
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:18.788
Today's goal: invite people, accept or decline, give wishes for birthdays, weddings and festivals, and make conversation at celebrations.

5
00:00:20.138 --> 00:00:20.991
Part 1.

6
00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:22.103
Inviting.

7
00:00:23.353 --> 00:00:26.020
We're having a small get-together on Saturday evening.

8
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.495
Would you like to come?

9
00:00:27.775 --> 00:00:29.823
It's my daughter's birthday on the 12th.

10
00:00:30.103 --> 00:00:31.852
We'd love it if you could join us.

11
00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:35.951
You're invited to our housewarming on Sunday, 1 pm onwards.

12
00:00:36.231 --> 00:00:38.129
Are you free for dinner next Friday?

13
00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:40.354
Part 2.

14
00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.127
Accepting and declining.

15
00:00:43.377 --> 00:00:44.743
Here is a quick table:

16
00:00:45.023 --> 00:00:46.857
Accept, and Decline politely.

17
00:00:47.137 --> 00:00:48.119
I'd love to!

18
00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:49.273
What time?:

19
00:00:49.553 --> 00:00:51.388
Thank you so much for inviting me.

20
00:00:51.668 --> 00:00:54.143
Unfortunately, I'm travelling that weekend.

21
00:00:54.423 --> 00:00:55.425
Sounds great.

22
00:00:55.705 --> 00:00:56.943
Can I bring anything?:

23
00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.612
I'm so sorry, I have a prior commitment.

24
00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.215
Let's catch up soon!

25
00:01:01.495 --> 00:01:02.433
Count me in!:

26
00:01:02.713 --> 00:01:05.124
I'd love to, but I can't make it this time.

27
00:01:05.404 --> 00:01:06.833
Have a wonderful evening!

28
00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:09.119
Thank you, we'll definitely be there.:

29
00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:10.700
I might be a little late.

30
00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.047
Is that okay?

31
00:01:13.397 --> 00:01:14.293
Part 3.

32
00:01:14.573 --> 00:01:16.173
Wishes for every occasion.

33
00:01:17.423 --> 00:01:18.788
Here is a quick table:

34
00:01:19.068 --> 00:01:20.647
Occasion, and What to say.

35
00:01:20.927 --> 00:01:21.759
Birthday:

36
00:01:22.039 --> 00:01:23.127
Happy birthday!

37
00:01:23.407 --> 00:01:25.369
Wishing you a wonderful year ahead.

38
00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:26.375
Wedding:

39
00:01:26.655 --> 00:01:27.913
Congratulations!

40
00:01:28.193 --> 00:01:30.391
Wishing you both a lifetime of happiness.

41
00:01:30.671 --> 00:01:31.673
Anniversary:

42
00:01:31.953 --> 00:01:33.233
Happy anniversary!

43
00:01:33.513 --> 00:01:35.327
Here's to many more years together.

44
00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:36.481
New baby:

45
00:01:36.761 --> 00:01:38.681
Congratulations on the little one!

46
00:01:38.961 --> 00:01:40.775
How are mother and baby doing?

47
00:01:41.055 --> 00:01:42.505
New job or promotion:

48
00:01:42.785 --> 00:01:44.044
Congratulations!

49
00:01:44.324 --> 00:01:45.625
You really deserve it.

50
00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:46.759
Festival:

51
00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:52.137
Happy Diwali! / Eid Mubarak! / Merry Christmas! / Happy Pongal!

52
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:55.063
Wishing you and your family joy and prosperity.

53
00:01:55.343 --> 00:01:56.303
Housewarming:

54
00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.481
Congratulations on the new home!

55
00:01:58.761 --> 00:01:59.935
It looks beautiful.

56
00:02:00.215 --> 00:02:01.132
Condolence:

57
00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:02.927
I'm so sorry for your loss.

58
00:02:03.207 --> 00:02:05.788
Please let me know if there's anything I can do.

59
00:02:07.138 --> 00:02:07.949
Get well:

60
00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:09.295
Get well soon!

61
00:02:09.575 --> 00:02:11.005
Take care and rest well.

62
00:02:12.355 --> 00:02:13.272
Part 4.

63
00:02:13.552 --> 00:02:16.027
Conversation 1: inviting a colleague.

64
00:02:17.277 --> 00:02:19.303
Here is how the conversation goes.

65
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:22.549
Hey Meena, are you free on Sunday evening?

66
00:02:22.829 --> 00:02:23.917
I think so.

67
00:02:24.197 --> 00:02:24.986
Why?

68
00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:28.253
We're having a housewarming party at our new flat.

69
00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:30.218
We'd love it if you could come.

70
00:02:30.498 --> 00:02:32.567
Congratulations on the new place!

71
00:02:32.847 --> 00:02:34.042
I'd love to.

72
00:02:34.322 --> 00:02:35.303
What time?

73
00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:37.269
Anytime after 6.

74
00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:39.341
I'll send you the location.

75
00:02:40.691 --> 00:02:42.291
The conversation continues.

76
00:02:42.571 --> 00:02:43.509
Great.

77
00:02:43.789 --> 00:02:45.240
Can I bring anything?

78
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.715
Just yourself!

79
00:02:46.995 --> 00:02:48.723
And your husband, of course.

80
00:02:49.003 --> 00:02:50.112
Thank you.

81
00:02:50.392 --> 00:02:51.779
We'll be there.

82
00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:54.089
Part 5.

83
00:02:54.369 --> 00:02:56.843
Conversation 2: at a wedding reception.

84
00:02:58.093 --> 00:03:00.120
Here is how the conversation goes.

85
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.341
Congratulations, Rahul!

86
00:03:02.621 --> 00:03:03.773
You look great.

87
00:03:04.053 --> 00:03:05.973
And congratulations, Divya!

88
00:03:06.253 --> 00:03:07.939
Thank you so much for coming!

89
00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:11.227
Divya, this is Ashish, my colleague from Bengaluru.

90
00:03:11.507 --> 00:03:12.744
Nice to meet you!

91
00:03:13.024 --> 00:03:15.008
Thank you for travelling all this way.

92
00:03:15.288 --> 00:03:16.440
It's a pleasure.

93
00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.661
The decorations are beautiful.

94
00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:21.480
Wishing you both a lifetime of happiness.

95
00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.430
The conversation continues.

96
00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:25.819
Thank you!

97
00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:27.955
Please have dinner before you leave.

98
00:03:28.235 --> 00:03:29.217
Definitely.

99
00:03:29.497 --> 00:03:32.611
Rahul, the photos from the sangeet looked amazing.

100
00:03:32.891 --> 00:03:34.001
You should have come!

101
00:03:34.281 --> 00:03:36.051
Next time, no excuses.

102
00:03:36.331 --> 00:03:37.697
Ha, I promise.

103
00:03:37.977 --> 00:03:39.342
Enjoy your evening!

104
00:03:40.692 --> 00:03:41.631
Part 6.

105
00:03:41.911 --> 00:03:43.340
Small talk at parties.

106
00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.891
How do you know the host?

107
00:03:46.171 --> 00:03:47.473
The food is amazing.

108
00:03:47.753 --> 00:03:49.182
Have you tried the desserts?

109
00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.126
Did you travel far to get here?

110
00:03:51.406 --> 00:03:52.835
It was lovely meeting you.

111
00:03:53.115 --> 00:03:54.715
I hope to see you again soon.

112
00:03:56.065 --> 00:03:57.004
Part 7.

113
00:03:57.284 --> 00:03:58.329
Speak today.

114
00:03:59.579 --> 00:04:03.035
Send one invitation or wish in English (WhatsApp counts).

115
00:04:03.315 --> 00:04:07.347
Practise declining politely with Thank you so much... unfortunately...

116
00:04:08.697 --> 00:04:10.233
That's the end of this lesson.

117
00:04:10.513 --> 00:04:15.185
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

118
00:04:15.465 --> 00:04:21.567
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

